  "notes": [
    {
      "content": "The page discusses axioms for ateliers based on the family F, M, or L. It says data on F are simplest and those on L most sophisticated, while essential axioms are less transparent on F and more transparent on L. It offers three choices of basic structure on F and explains the collection map as deployment/incidence. A later dated note objects that choice b) no longer implies ≪ from the author’s new point of view. The closing paragraph promises a diagram of six fundamental relations and defines the incidence symbol by F ≤ G together with F ∈ M.",
      "math_reading_decisions": "The list is an aligned list, not a diagram. Straight ≤ and double left angles ≪ differ from the curved subdivision sign in b). The underbrace begins under et, not under ≪. P is a plain upright letter in this page’s map; F ↦ F̃ has an initial mapping bar and tilde. The last definition has a closed left triangle and a double implication. Singular le plus transparent and the spelling déployement are preserved without mathematical or grammatical repair. The cancellation layers at the right are represented, and low-confidence material remains marked. Exact alphabet choices for F and M remain open at first occurrence.",
      "author_doubts": [
        "(ou peut-être pareil pour M ?)",
        "(20-juin [separator uncertain]) Non, par mon nouveau point de vue ça n’implique plus ≪"
      ],
      "titles_dates_counts": "Underlined title Axiomes; underlined Sur F. Manuscript page number 10. Formula labels (1.16) and (1.17). Three alternatives a), b), c); the prose says six relations, but their promised diagram is not yet on this page. Dated note says 20 juin, with an uncertain separator. No archive pencil sheet number is visible."
    }
